fix(kanban): resolve infinite render loop and restore native inline card creation

WHAT:
- ColIdInjector: fixed dependency-less useEffect that called setHeaders unconditionally
  every render cycle — added deep equality check so setState only fires when DOM
  headers actually change (length or id mismatch)
- Removed custom sqhq-custom-add-btn portal injection from column headers
- Removed addCard() callback and CardEditor modal triggered from column header
- Removed CSS rule hiding .wx-add (SVAR's native inline add button) via display:none
- NotesKanban cardContent: mapped props.card.text -> card.label so natively created
  SVAR cards are not blank when they appear in our custom KanbanCard renderer

WHY:
The ColIdInjector ran setHeaders inside setTimeout with no deps every 50ms causing
React's reconciler to loop continuously, producing severe input lag and interaction
freezes across the entire board. The custom add modal was also anti-native —
replacing SVAR's built-in inline card creation with a center-screen floating form
broke the expected Trello/Linear workflow of typing a title and pressing Enter.

FILES: NotesKanban.tsx, kanban-dark.css
